<h3>My Array</h3>
<p id="a07e67e4-5a02-4b59-ae4c-1c6ef8035771" class=""><strong>Exercise</strong>: Create some objects using the same model
    you created on the MyObjects page. Populate three more of them with three more books from the 10 Books Exercise. Put each of the objects in its
    own index in an Array and dump it out. Are you starting to see how an array of objects can be a powerful
    thing? If not, no stress but stay tuned. I know that this exercise is repetitive. In a few screens we are
    going to see how we can make the computer create the objects and arrays we want more easily and
    automatically. For now though, just type it out.</p>


<h3>My Array</h3>

<bx:set allMyBooks = [

    {
        title: "Ninth House",
        length: 480,
        yearPublished: 2020,
        publisher: {
            name: "Flatiron Books"
        },
        format: "Paperback",
        author: {
            firstName: "Leigh",
            lastName: "Bardugo"
        },
        genres: ["Dark Fantasy"],
        language: "English",
        condition: "Good",
        publicationCountry: "United States",
        price: 19.99
    },

    {
        title: "Dune",
        length: 896,
        yearPublished: 1965,
        publisher: {
            name: "Ace Books"
        },
        format: "Paperback",
        author: {
            firstName: "Frank",
            lastName: "Herbert"
        },
        genres: ["Science Fiction"],
        language: "English",
        condition: "Fair",
        publicationCountry: "United States",
        price: 20.00
    },

    {
        title: "Burmese Days",
        length: 287,
        yearPublished: 1934,
        publisher: {
            name: "Harcourt. Inc"
        },
        format: "Paperback",
        author: {
            firstName: "George",
            lastName: "Orwell"
        },
        genres: ["Historical Fiction"],
        language: "English",
        condition: "Good",
        publicationCountry: "United States",
        price: 18.99
    },

    {
        title: "Eragon",
        length: 544,
        yearPublished: 2003,
        publisher: {
            name: "Knopf Books for Young Readers"
        },
        format: "Paperback",
        author: {
            firstName: "Christopher",
            lastName: "Paolini"
        },
        genres: ["Fantasy"],
        language: "English",
        condition: "Fair",
        publicationCountry: "United States",
        price: 15.99
    },

    {
        title: "Snow",
        length: 304,
        yearPublished: 2020,
        publisher: {
            name: "Hanover Square Press"
        },
        format: "Paperback",
        author: {
            firstName: "John",
            lastName: "Banville"
        },
        genres: ["Literary Fiction"],
        language: "English",
        condition: "Great",
        publicationCountry: "United States",
        price: 16.99
    }

] />

<bx:set totalCost = 0 />

<bx:output>

    <bx:loop array="#allMyBooks#" item="book">

        <p><strong>Title:</strong> #book.title#</p>

        <p><strong>Length:</strong> #book.length# pages</p>

        <p><strong>Year Published:</strong> #book.yearPublished#</p>

        <p><strong>Publisher:</strong> #book.publisher.name#</p>

        <p><strong>Format:</strong> #book.format#</p>

        <p><strong>Author:</strong>
            #book.author.firstName# #book.author.lastName#
        </p>

        <p><strong>Genres:</strong> #book.genres.join(", ")#</p>

        <p><strong>Language:</strong> #book.language#</p>

        <p><strong>Book Condition:</strong> #book.condition#</p>

        <p><strong>Publication Country:</strong> #book.publicationCountry#</p>

        <p><strong>Price:</strong> $#numberFormat(book.price, "0.00")#</p>

        <hr />

        <bx:set totalCost = totalCost + book.price />

    </bx:loop>

    <h3>Total Cost: $#numberFormat(totalCost, "0.00")#</h3>

</bx:output>




